# IGNORE-BY-DEFAULT, then name what is kept. The source tree this repo was
# curated from is 74 GB across ~50,000 files; the code and records are a rounding
# error inside it. "Everything, then name what we drop" fails open, and the
# failure is someone committing 26 GB of adapters and nobody noticing until the
# next clone. So: nothing, then re-include.
*
!*/

# What is kept: source, records, plans, procedures, small figures, web assets.
!*.py
!*.sh
!*.js
!*.css
!*.html
!*.md
!*.json
!*.jsonl
!*.txt
!*.tab
!*.csv
!*.yaml
!*.yml
!*.svg
!*.png
!.gitignore
!requirements.txt

# Bulk, listed AFTER the re-includes so these win. Written WITHOUT a leading slash
# and WITHOUT an interior slash so they match at any depth: `adapters/` is
# unanchored; `adapters/**` (interior slash) silently anchors to the repo root and
# stops matching sweep100/adapters/. That trap bit the original repo once.
.venv/
.venv_*/
__pycache__/
vendor/
shots/
backups/
node_modules/

# Weights and arrays never go in git: the zoo is on the Hub
# (EternalRecursion/persona-lora-zoo-qwen35) and the analysis arrays are on the
# results dataset (EternalRecursion/persona-curvature-results, restored by
# tools/fetch_data.py). Directory rules are CONTENTS-ONLY (`x/**` + `!x/**/`) so
# the per-run runmeta*.json records inside them can still be re-included below:
# git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a re-include beneath one
# can never fire unless the directory itself stays traversable.
*.safetensors
*.npz
*.npy
*.pkl
*.pt
*.bin
*.parquet
*.zip
*.enc
**/adapters/**
!**/adapters/**/
**/adapters_sft/**
!**/adapters_sft/**/
**/adapters_smoke_evidence/**
!**/adapters_smoke_evidence/**/
**/phase2_adapters*/**
!**/phase2_adapters*/**/
qwen35/*_files/**
!qwen35/*_files/**/

# Hosted on the results dataset, not in git (see docs/DATA.md). Same contents-only
# form: the four runmeta*.json records in qwen35/results/ come back below.
qwen35/analysis/**
!qwen35/analysis/**/
qwen35/results/**
!qwen35/results/**/
qwen35/data/**
!qwen35/data/**/
qwen35/data_*/**
!qwen35/data_*/**/
qwen35/phase10_runs/**
!qwen35/phase10_runs/**/

# Pre-zoo training corpora (sweep100, ~244 MB of jsonl): left out of git and out
# of the results dataset; available on request. See docs/HISTORY.md.
sweep100/data/**
sweep100/data_bal/**
sweep100/data_expanded/**
sweep100/data_bal_expanded/**

# Logs, stdout captures, editor backups, build stamps, smoke and discarded runs.
*.log
*.log.*
*.out
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak-*
*.bak_*
*.bak[0-9]*
*.withdrawn-backup
*DISCARDED*
.build_stamp
.last_status
.s2_reported
smoke_data/
results_smoke/
results_synth/
*_smoke.json

# Generated pages that are rebuilt from the analysis files. The two exceptions
# (qwen35/spider_page/index.html, qwen35/sphere_page/index_fa.html) are inputs to
# wiki/tools/build_site.py and are not listed here.
qwen35/blog_page/index.html
qwen35/site/index.html
qwen35/site_traits/index.html
qwen35/live_page/index.html
qwen35/zoo_page/index.html
qwen35/findings_page/index.html
qwen35/manifold_page/index.html
qwen35/monitor_page/index.html
qwen35/distil_page/index.html
qwen35/direction_pages/*.html
sweep100/site/data.json
qwen35/companion/vendor/

# What tools/fetch_data.py leaves behind besides the restored files: huggingface_hub's
# download metadata at the repo root, and adapters fetched with --zoo.
.cache/
qwen35/adapters_zoo/

# Files over 5 MB that would otherwise pass the extension rules. A .gitignore
# cannot enforce a size cap; these are the known offenders, and the check below
# is what actually enforces it.
qwen35/figures/clusters/gallery*.html
qwen35/figures/clusters/*.png

# The three 2026-09-15 POST_DRAFT backups the draft cites are the only .bak files kept.
!qwen35/POST_DRAFT_2026-09-15_*.bak.md

# Per-run provenance (seed, hyperparameters, cost) lives INSIDE the adapter
# directories, which is why those rules above are contents-only. Only the run
# RECORDS come back, not adapter_config.json or the 19 MB tokenizer.json.
!**/runmeta*.json

# The companion builder's cached stage-two excerpts (one row per trait, 134 small
# JSON files) are a build input, not a cache to drop; stated explicitly so a later
# `cache/` rule cannot silently take them.
!qwen35/companion/cache/**

# ASSERT AFTER ANY CHANGE TO THIS FILE -- do not eyeball whether "some appeared":
#   disk=$(find . -name 'runmeta*.json' -not -path '*/.venv*' -not -path './.git/*' | wc -l)
#   trk=$(git ls-files | grep -c 'runmeta.*\.json')        # disk and trk MUST be equal (234)
#   git ls-files -z | xargs -0 du -b | awk '$1 > 5000000'    # MUST print nothing
#   git ls-files | grep -E '\.(safetensors|npz|npy|pkl|pt)$' # MUST print nothing

# Cited by wiki pages zoo/discarded-secondary-draws and zoo/constitution-anchor-revision:
# the two discarded secondary-trait draws and the three constitution snapshots
# taken before each anchor revision. Small (under 1 MB each), part of the record.
!qwen35/traits_secondary_DISCARDED_draw*.json
!qwen35/backups/
!qwen35/backups/constitutions.json.*.bak
